 day £480.00; Licence per user per month £14.20."}],"reviewed":false},{"id":"X-C-024-serviceCredits","contractId":"C-024","questionId":"Q8","fieldKey":"serviceCredits","answer":{"present":true,"perFailurePct":0.02,"monthlyCapPct":0.1},"answerType":"service_credits","status":"found","confidence":0.94,"provenance":[{"documentId":"DOC-C-024","page":50,"clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","quote":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges."}],"reviewed":false},{"id":"X-C-024-terminationForConvenience","contractId":"C-024","questionId":"Q9","fieldKey":"terminationForConvenience","answer":{"allowed":true,"noticeMonths":3},"answerType":"termination","status":"found","confidence":0.93,"provenance":[{"documentId":"DOC-C-024","page":30,"clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","quote":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice."}],"reviewed":false},{"id":"X-C-024-exitFees","contractId":"C-024","questionId":"Q9","fieldKey":"exitFees","answer":{"present":false,"summary":"None"},"answerType":"exit_fees","status":"found","confidence":0.94,"provenance":[{"documentId":"DOC-C-024","page":32,"clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","quote":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date."}],"reviewed":false}],"documents":{"DOC-C-001":{"id":"DOC-C-001","contractId":"C-001","title":"Integrated facilities management: agreement","pageCount":54,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"3":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 3 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd, company number 90010000."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Integrated facilities management, being hard and soft facilities services across the Council's operational buildings, including planned and reactive maintenance, security, cleaning and grounds."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 April 2022.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-001-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 March 2027.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-001-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £2,400,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-001-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £12,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-001-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"9":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 9 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The Council may, by giving the Supplier written notice, extend the Term on 2 occasions by up to 12 months each time (each an Extension Period).","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-001-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"The decision to extend is the Council's alone. The Supplier may not refuse an extension that the Council has validly exercised."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 March 2029."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term include any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.7","title":"No compensation","text":"The Supplier is not entitled to compensation if the Council decides not to extend the Term."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"16":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 16 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-001, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-001-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.7","title":"Set-off","text":"The Council may set off any sum the Supplier owes the Council against a sum due to the Supplier under this Agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"19":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 19 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for the Services delivered each month, less any Service Credits deducted under Schedule 6."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £12,000,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-001-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £9,600,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.6","title":"No minimum commitment","text":"The Council is not obliged to purchase any minimum volume of Services, and the estimated values in the Contract Particulars do not create a minimum commitment."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.7","title":"Approval of a Variation","text":"A Variation that increases the Maximum Contract Value takes effect only when it has been agreed in writing and signed for the Council by an officer with authority under its Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"27":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 27 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-001-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.7","title":"Performance during notice","text":"During any notice period the Supplier shall continue to perform the Services in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"28":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 28 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-001-noticePeriod","X-C-001-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 30 September 2026."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.7","title":"Receipt","text":"A notice is treated as received on the day of delivery by hand, or on the second Working Day after posting."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 29 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"On early termination the Council shall pay: Unamortised mobilisation costs, reducing monthly over the Initial Term.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-001-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.7","title":"Handover","text":"The Supplier shall keep the asset register and planned maintenance schedules up to date until the exit date and hand them to the Council or its replacement supplier."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"39":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 39 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Operative per hour £19.40; Supervisor per hour £27.85; Out-of-hours call-out per call £145.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-001-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"clause","num":"6","title":"Out of hours","text":"An out-of-hours rate applies only to work that the Council has asked the Supplier to carry out outside normal working hours."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"42":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 42 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 April each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 3.0% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-001-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Late evidence","text":"If the Supplier does not give the evidence required by paragraph 2.2 by the review date, the Charges stay the same until the next review date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}],"47":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Integrated facilities management: agreement | Page 47 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-001-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Deduction","text":"Service Credits shall be deducted from the next invoice, or paid by the Supplier within thirty (30) days if no further invoice is due."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.4","title":"Overall limit","text":"The limit of 10% of the monthly Charges applies to all Service Credits in a month taken together."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-001 | Kestrelvale Facilities Services Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-002":{"id":"DOC-C-002","contractId":"C-002","title":"Domiciliary care call-off: agreement","pageCount":58,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"4":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 4 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd, company number 90010137."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Domiciliary care call-off."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 April 2023.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-002-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 March 2028.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-002-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Framework call-off."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £2,900,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-002-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £14,500,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-002-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"10":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 10 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The parties may agree in writing to extend the Term on 1 occasion by up to 24 months each time.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-002-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"An extension takes effect only if both parties have agreed it in writing before the notice date in clause 31.1."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 March 2030."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term include any Extension Period."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"17":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 17 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-002, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 28 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-002-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"20":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 20 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for Services properly performed in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £16,000,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-002-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £12,800,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.6","title":"No minimum commitment","text":"The Council is not obliged to purchase any minimum volume of Services, and the estimated values in the Contract Particulars do not create a minimum commitment."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"28":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 28 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-002-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 29 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than twelve (12) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-002-noticePeriod","X-C-002-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 31 March 2027."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 30 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-002-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"40":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 40 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Standard care visit per hour £24.60; Evening and weekend per hour £28.90; Night sleep-in per night £118.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-002-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"43":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 43 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 April each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 4.0% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-002-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}],"48":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Domiciliary care call-off: agreement | Page 48 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-002-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Deduction","text":"Service Credits shall be deducted from the next invoice, or paid by the Supplier within thirty (30) days if no further invoice is due."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-002 | Wrenfield Care Partners Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-003":{"id":"DOC-C-003","contractId":"C-003","title":"Waste collection and recycling: agreement","pageCount":62,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"5":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 5 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Quillon Waste Services Ltd, company number 90010274."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Waste collection and recycling."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 February 2019.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-003-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 January 2027.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-003-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £6,200,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-003-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £49,600,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-003-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"No maximum contract value is stated. The estimated total value above is the only value limit in the Agreement.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 10","extractionIds":["X-C-003-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"11","text":"The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"11":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 11 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"There is no right to extend the Term beyond the Expiry Date.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-003-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Re-procurement","text":"The Council shall decide before the notice date in clause 31.1 whether to procure a replacement for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"No implied extension","text":"Nothing in this Agreement entitles the Supplier to carry out Services, or to be paid for them, after the Expiry Date unless the parties agree a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Further contracts","text":"Any further contract for the Services shall be awarded in accordance with the Council's Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"18":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 18 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-003, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-003-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 29 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-003-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 30 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"Unless the Council gives the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term, this Agreement shall renew automatically for a further period of 12 months.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-003-noticePeriod","X-C-003-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Renewal terms","text":"Where this Agreement renews under clause 31.1, the renewed term is on the same terms and the Charges are reviewed in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 31 October 2026."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"No reasons needed","text":"The Council may give notice under clause 31.1 without giving reasons and without liability to pay compensation to the Supplier."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 31 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"On early termination the Council shall pay: Unamortised vehicle costs, up to £1.2m.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-003-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"41":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 41 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Residual collection per tonne £68.50; Dry recycling per tonne £22.40; Bulky waste per item £17.50.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-003-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"44":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 44 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 February each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 4.0% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-003-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}],"49":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Waste collection and recycling: agreement | Page 49 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-003-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-003 | Quillon Waste Services Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-004":{"id":"DOC-C-004","contractId":"C-004","title":"Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement","pageCount":66,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"6":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 6 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd, company number 90010411."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Street lighting and signage maintenance, being routine and reactive maintenance of street lighting columns, illuminated signs and bollards, and the replacement of lanterns across the Council's highway network."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 August 2022.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-004-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 July 2027.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-004-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £2,200,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-004-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £11,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-004-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"12":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 12 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The Council may, by giving the Supplier written notice, extend the Term on 1 occasion by up to 12 months each time (each an Extension Period).","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-004-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"The decision to extend is the Council's alone. The Supplier may not refuse an extension that the Council has validly exercised."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 July 2028."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term include any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.7","title":"No compensation","text":"The Supplier is not entitled to compensation if the Council decides not to extend the Term."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"19":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 19 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-004, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-004-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.7","title":"Set-off","text":"The Council may set off any sum the Supplier owes the Council against a sum due to the Supplier under this Agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"22":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 22 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for lighting units maintained and works completed, measured against the inventory of lighting assets held by the Council."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £11,000,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-004-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £8,800,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.6","title":"No minimum commitment","text":"The Council is not obliged to purchase any minimum volume of Services, and the estimated values in the Contract Particulars do not create a minimum commitment."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.7","title":"Approval of a Variation","text":"A Variation that increases the Maximum Contract Value takes effect only when it has been agreed in writing and signed for the Council by an officer with authority under its Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 30 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-004-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.7","title":"Performance during notice","text":"During any notice period the Supplier shall continue to perform the Services in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 31 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-004-noticePeriod","X-C-004-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 31 January 2027."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.7","title":"Receipt","text":"A notice is treated as received on the day of delivery by hand, or on the second Working Day after posting."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"32":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 32 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-004-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.7","title":"Handover","text":"The Supplier shall hand over the lighting asset inventory, test certificates and defect logs to the Council in an agreed electronic format."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"42":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 42 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Operative per hour £31.20; Gang with vehicle per hour £96.00; Lantern replacement per unit £188.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-004-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"clause","num":"6","title":"Out of hours","text":"An out-of-hours rate applies only to work that the Council has asked the Supplier to carry out outside normal working hours."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"45":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 45 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 August each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 3.0% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-004-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Late evidence","text":"If the Supplier does not give the evidence required by paragraph 2.2 by the review date, the Charges stay the same until the next review date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}],"50":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Street lighting and signage maintenance: agreement | Page 50 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-004-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Deduction","text":"Service Credits shall be deducted from the next invoice, or paid by the Supplier within thirty (30) days if no further invoice is due."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.4","title":"Overall limit","text":"The limit of 10% of the monthly Charges applies to all Service Credits in a month taken together."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-004 | Ordwell Lighting and Signs Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-005":{"id":"DOC-C-005","contractId":"C-005","title":"Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement","pageCount":70,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"7":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 7 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Fennimore Highways Ltd, company number 90010548."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Highways reactive maintenance and minor works, being reactive repairs, emergency make-safe works and minor works orders across the Council's adopted highway network."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 June 2022.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-005-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 May 2027.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-005-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £1,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-005-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £5,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-005-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"13":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 13 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"There is no right to extend the Term beyond the Expiry Date.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-005-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Re-procurement","text":"The Council shall decide before the notice date in clause 31.1 whether to procure a replacement for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"No implied extension","text":"Nothing in this Agreement entitles the Supplier to carry out Services, or to be paid for them, after the Expiry Date unless the parties agree a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Further contracts","text":"Any further contract for the Services shall be awarded in accordance with the Council's Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term are to the period from the Commencement Date to the Expiry Date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.7","title":"No compensation","text":"The Supplier is not entitled to compensation when the Term ends on the Expiry Date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"20":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 20 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-005, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-005-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.7","title":"Set-off","text":"The Council may set off any sum the Supplier owes the Council against a sum due to the Supplier under this Agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"23":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 23 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges for each Order completed to the specification, priced from the Schedule of Rates in Schedule 3 and certified by the Council's Highways Manager."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £5,000,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-005-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £4,000,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.6","title":"No minimum commitment","text":"The Council is not obliged to purchase any minimum volume of Services, and the estimated values in the Contract Particulars do not create a minimum commitment."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.7","title":"Approval of a Variation","text":"A Variation that increases the Maximum Contract Value takes effect only when it has been agreed in writing and signed for the Council by an officer with authority under its Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 31 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-005-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.7","title":"Performance during notice","text":"During any notice period the Supplier shall continue to perform the Services in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"32":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 32 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-005-noticePeriod","X-C-005-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 28 February 2027."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.7","title":"Receipt","text":"A notice is treated as received on the day of delivery by hand, or on the second Working Day after posting."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"33":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 33 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-005-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.7","title":"Handover","text":"The Supplier shall complete or make safe every open Order before the exit date, and hand its records of inspections and defects to the Council."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"43":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 43 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Operative per hour £31.20; Gang with vehicle per hour £96.00; Lantern replacement per unit £188.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-005-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are fixed for the Initial Term."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"clause","num":"6","title":"Out of hours","text":"An out-of-hours rate applies only to work that the Council has asked the Supplier to carry out outside normal working hours."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"46":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 46 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges are fixed for the Initial Term and are not subject to indexation.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-005-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Requests to change","text":"Any request to change the Charges during the Initial Term must follow clause 41 (Variation)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No change for the Supplier's costs","text":"Nothing in this Schedule 4 permits an increase because of changes in the Supplier's own costs, including labour, plant, materials and fuel."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Agreement in writing","text":"The Council shall not be required to pay an increase in the Charges that has not been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Inclusive Charges","text":"The Charges include all costs of delivering the Services, including labour, plant and materials."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}],"51":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Highways reactive maintenance and minor works: agreement | Page 51 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"No service credit regime applies under this Agreement.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-005-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Other remedies","text":"The Council's remedies for poor performance are set out in clause 22 (Performance management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Repeated failure","text":"Repeated failure to meet a Key Performance Indicator is a Performance Failure and shall be dealt with under clause 22."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.4","title":"Escalation","text":"The Council may escalate a Performance Failure to the Supplier's senior management under clause 22."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-005 | Fennimore Highways Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-006":{"id":"DOC-C-006","contractId":"C-006","title":"Leisure centres management: agreement","pageCount":74,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"3":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 3 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Brindlemere Leisure Trust, company number 90010685."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Leisure centres management."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 April 2022.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-006-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 March 2032.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-006-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Concession."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £1,100,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-006-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £11,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-006-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"No maximum contract value is stated. The estimated total value above is the only value limit in the Agreement.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 10","extractionIds":["X-C-006-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"11","text":"The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"9":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 9 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The parties may agree in writing to extend the Term on 1 occasion by up to 60 months each time.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-006-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"An extension takes effect only if both parties have agreed it in writing before the notice date in clause 31.1."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 March 2037."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term include any Extension Period."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"16":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 16 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council quarterly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-006, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-006-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"27":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 27 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"Neither party may terminate this Agreement for convenience.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-006-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Routes to early exit","text":"Because neither party may terminate for convenience, the Council's routes to early exit are those in clauses 30.2 to 30.4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"28":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 28 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than twelve (12) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-006-noticePeriod","X-C-006-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 31 March 2031."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 29 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"On early termination the Council shall pay: Fixed termination sum of £450,000 in years 1 to 5.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-006-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"39":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 39 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Standard rate per hour £42.00; Senior rate per hour £68.00; Out-of-hours call-out per call £145.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-006-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"42":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 42 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 April each year by reference to the Retail Prices Index (RPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 3.5% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-006-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}],"47":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Leisure centres management: agreement | Page 47 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"No service credit regime applies under this Agreement.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-006-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Other remedies","text":"The Council's remedies for poor performance are set out in clause 22 (Performance management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Repeated failure","text":"Repeated failure to meet a Key Performance Indicator is a Performance Failure and shall be dealt with under clause 22."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-006 | Brindlemere Leisure Trust"}]}},"DOC-C-007":{"id":"DOC-C-007","contractId":"C-007","title":"ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement","pageCount":78,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"4":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 4 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Pellam Digital Ltd, company number 90010822."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: ICT managed service and end-user support."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 May 2023.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-007-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 30 April 2026.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-007-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Framework call-off."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £1,800,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-007-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £5,400,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-007-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"10":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 10 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The Council may, by giving the Supplier written notice, extend the Term on 2 occasions by up to 12 months each time (each an Extension Period).","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-007-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"The decision to extend is the Council's alone. The Supplier may not refuse an extension that the Council has validly exercised."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 30 April 2028."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"17":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 17 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-007, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-007-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"20":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 20 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for Services properly performed in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £5,400,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-007-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £4,320,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"28":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 28 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-007-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 29 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-007-noticePeriod","X-C-007-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 30 January 2026."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 30 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-007-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"40":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 40 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Service desk analyst per day £310.00; Engineer per day £480.00; Licence per user per month £14.20.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-007-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are fixed for the Initial Term."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"43":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 43 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges are fixed for the Initial Term and are not subject to indexation.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-007-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Requests to change","text":"Any request to change the Charges during the Initial Term must follow clause 41 (Variation)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No change for the Supplier's costs","text":"Nothing in this Schedule 4 permits an increase because of changes in the Supplier's own costs, including labour, plant, materials and fuel."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}],"48":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | ICT managed service and end-user support: agreement | Page 48 of 78"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-007-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-007 | Pellam Digital Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-008":{"id":"DOC-C-008","contractId":"C-008","title":"Housing repairs and voids: agreement","pageCount":54,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"5":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 5 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Ashmere Property Services Ltd, company number 90010959."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Housing repairs and voids."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 April 2024.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-008-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 March 2029.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-008-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £4,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-008-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £20,000,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-008-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"11":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 11 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The parties may agree in writing to extend the Term on 2 occasions by up to 12 months each time.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-008-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"An extension takes effect only if both parties have agreed it in writing before the notice date in clause 31.1."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 March 2031."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term include any Extension Period."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"18":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 18 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-008, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-008-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"21":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 21 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for Services properly performed in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £22,000,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-008-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £17,600,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.6","title":"No minimum commitment","text":"The Council is not obliged to purchase any minimum volume of Services, and the estimated values in the Contract Particulars do not create a minimum commitment."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 29 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-008-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 30 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-008-noticePeriod","X-C-008-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 30 September 2028."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 31 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"On early termination the Council shall pay: Unamortised mobilisation costs.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-008-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"41":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 41 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Standard rate per hour £42.00; Senior rate per hour £68.00; Out-of-hours call-out per call £145.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-008-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"44":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 44 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 April each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 3.0% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-008-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}],"49":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Housing repairs and voids: agreement | Page 49 of 54"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-008-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Deduction","text":"Service Credits shall be deducted from the next invoice, or paid by the Supplier within thirty (30) days if no further invoice is due."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-008 | Ashmere Property Services Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-009":{"id":"DOC-C-009","contractId":"C-009","title":"Grounds maintenance: agreement","pageCount":58,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"6":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Grounds maintenance: agreement | Page 6 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Larchmont Grounds Ltd, company number 90011096."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Grounds maintenance."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 April 2022.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-009-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 March 2027.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-009-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £420,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-009-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £2,100,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-009-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-009 | Larchmont Grounds Ltd"}],"12":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Grounds maintenance: agreement | Page 12 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The Council may, by giving the Supplier written notice, extend the Term on 1 occasion by up to 12 months each time (each an Extension Period).","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-009-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"The decision to extend is the Council's alone. The Supplier may not refuse an extension that the Council has validly exercised."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 March 2028."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-009 | Larchmont Grounds Ltd"}],"19":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Grounds maintenance: agreement | Page 19 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-009, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-009-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-009 | Larchmont Grounds Ltd"}],"22":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Grounds maintenance: agreement | Page 22 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for Services properly performed in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £2,200,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-009-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £1,760,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-009 | Larchmont Grounds Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Grounds maintenance: agreement | Page 30 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-009-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-009 | Larchmont Grounds Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Grounds maintenance: agreement | Page 31 of 58"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the 