","extractionIds":["X-C-010-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Social care case management software: agreement | Page 31 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-010-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}],"32":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Social care case management software: agreement | Page 32 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"Unless the Council gives the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term, this Agreement shall renew automatically for a further period of 12 months.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-010-noticePeriod","X-C-010-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Renewal terms","text":"Where this Agreement renews under clause 31.1, the renewed term is on the same terms and the Charges are reviewed in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 30 June 2028."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"No reasons needed","text":"The Council may give notice under clause 31.1 without giving reasons and without liability to pay compensation to the Supplier."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}],"33":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Social care case management software: agreement | Page 33 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"On early termination the Council shall pay: Licence fees for the remainder of the paid year are not refundable.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-010-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}],"43":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Social care case management software: agreement | Page 43 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Service desk analyst per day £310.00; Engineer per day £480.00; Licence per user per month £14.20.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-010-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}],"46":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Social care case management software: agreement | Page 46 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 January each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 3.0% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-010-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}],"51":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Social care case management software: agreement | Page 51 of 62"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-010-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Deduction","text":"Service Credits shall be deducted from the next invoice, or paid by the Supplier within thirty (30) days if no further invoice is due."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-010 | Hexmoor Software Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-011":{"id":"DOC-C-011","contractId":"C-011","title":"Legal services panel: agreement","pageCount":66,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"3":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 3 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Westerfield Legal LLP, company number 90011370."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Legal services panel."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 April 2023.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-011-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 March 2028.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-011-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Direct award."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £420,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-011-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £2,100,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-011-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Annual Cap: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"9":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 9 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"There is no right to extend the Term beyond the Expiry Date.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-011-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Re-procurement","text":"The Council shall decide before the notice date in clause 31.1 whether to procure a replacement for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"No implied extension","text":"Nothing in this Agreement entitles the Supplier to carry out Services, or to be paid for them, after the Expiry Date unless the parties agree a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Further contracts","text":"Any further contract for the Services shall be awarded in accordance with the Council's Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"16":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 16 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-011, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-011-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"19":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 19 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Annual Cap"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for Services properly performed in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Annual Cap","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £450,000 in any Contract Year (the Annual Cap) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-011-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges in a Contract Year reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Annual Cap, being £360,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Annual Cap to be exceeded in a Contract Year unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"27":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 27 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than one (1) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-011-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"28":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 28 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-011-noticePeriod","X-C-011-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 31 December 2027."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 29 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-011-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"39":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 39 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Standard rate per hour £42.00; Senior rate per hour £68.00; Out-of-hours call-out per call £145.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-011-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"42":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 42 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 April each year by reference to the Consumer Prices Index (CPI) for the preceding September.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-011-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}],"47":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Legal services panel: agreement | Page 47 of 66"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"No service credit regime applies under this Agreement.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-011-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Other remedies","text":"The Council's remedies for poor performance are set out in clause 22 (Performance management)."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-011 | Westerfield Legal LLP"}]}},"DOC-C-012":{"id":"DOC-C-012","contractId":"C-012","title":"Home-to-school transport: agreement","pageCount":70,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"4":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 4 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd, company number 90011507."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: Home-to-school transport."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 September 2022.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-012-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 August 2029.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-012-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Dynamic purchasing system."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £1,700,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-012-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £11,900,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-012-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"Maximum Contract Value: see clause 14.3. The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"10":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 10 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"There is no right to extend the Term beyond the Expiry Date.","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-012-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Re-procurement","text":"The Council shall decide before the notice date in clause 31.1 whether to procure a replacement for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"No implied extension","text":"Nothing in this Agreement entitles the Supplier to carry out Services, or to be paid for them, after the Expiry Date unless the parties agree a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Further contracts","text":"Any further contract for the Services shall be awarded in accordance with the Council's Contract Procedure Rules."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.6","title":"Interpretation","text":"References to the Term are to the period from the Commencement Date to the Expiry Date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"17":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 17 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-012, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-012-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.6","title":"Disputed invoices","text":"If the Council disputes part of an invoice it shall pay the undisputed part and tell the Supplier within ten (10) days why it disputes the rest."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"20":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 20 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"14","text":"Charges and Maximum Contract Value"},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.1","title":"Charges","text":"The Council shall pay the Charges set out in Schedule 2 for Services properly performed in accordance with this Agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.2","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT and are the only sums payable by the Council for the Services."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.3","title":"Maximum Contract Value","text":"The Council's liability to pay the Charges under this Agreement shall not exceed £12,500,000 in aggregate (the Maximum Contract Value) unless increased by a Variation under clause 41.","clauseRef":"Clause 14.3","extractionIds":["X-C-012-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.4","title":"Alert at 80%","text":"The Supplier shall notify the Council in writing when cumulative Charges reach eighty per cent (80%) of the Maximum Contract Value, being £10,000,000."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.5","title":"Services beyond the limit","text":"The Supplier shall not be obliged to perform Services that would cause the Maximum Contract Value to be exceeded unless a Variation has been agreed in writing under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"14.6","title":"No minimum commitment","text":"The Council is not obliged to purchase any minimum volume of Services, and the estimated values in the Contract Particulars do not create a minimum commitment."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"28":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 28 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-012-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.6","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination does not affect any right that has accrued before the termination date."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 29 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than six (6) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-012-noticePeriod","X-C-012-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 28 February 2029."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.6","title":"Register","text":"The Council shall record the last date for notice in its contracts register."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 30 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.2","title":"Payments on termination","text":"No termination payment is due from the Council except for Charges properly incurred up to the termination date.","clauseRef":"Clause 33.2","extractionIds":["X-C-012-exitFees"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.3","title":"Exit assistance","text":"On expiry or termination the Supplier shall give the Council the exit assistance described in Schedule 9 (Exit management)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.4","title":"Return of property","text":"The Supplier shall return all Council data and property within thirty (30) days of the date of termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.5","title":"Survival","text":"Clauses 11 (Confidentiality), 33 and 44 (Governing law) survive termination or expiry."},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.6","title":"Staff","text":"Where staff transfer on exit, the parties shall comply with the provisions in Schedule 10 (Staff transfer)."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"40":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 40 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 3","text":"Schedule of rates"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1","title":"Application","text":"The rates in Table 1 apply to Services ordered during the Initial Term and any Extension Period."},{"kind":"clause","num":"Table 1","title":"Rates","text":"Schedule of rates: Standard rate per hour £42.00; Senior rate per hour £68.00; Out-of-hours call-out per call £145.00.","clauseRef":"Schedule 3, Table 1","extractionIds":["X-C-012-rateCard"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2","title":"VAT","text":"All rates are exclusive of VAT."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3","title":"Review of rates","text":"The rates are reviewed once a year in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"4","title":"Additional work","text":"Work that is not covered by Table 1 shall be priced pro rata from the nearest equivalent rate and agreed in writing before the work starts."},{"kind":"clause","num":"5","title":"Travel","text":"The Council shall not be charged for travel time or mobilisation unless Table 1 says so."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"43":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 43 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 4","text":"Price review"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Starting Charges","text":"The Charges at the Commencement Date are set out in Schedule 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.2","title":"Changes","text":"The Charges may be changed only under this Schedule 4 or by a Variation under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Annual review","text":"The Charges shall be reviewed on 1 September each year by reference to the Retail Prices Index (RPI) for the preceding September, provided that no increase shall exceed 4.5% in any Contract Year.","clauseRef":"Schedule 4, paragraph 2.1","extractionIds":["X-C-012-indexation"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Evidence","text":"The Supplier shall send the Council the index figures it has used, with its calculation, at least thirty (30) days before the review date."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"No retrospective increase","text":"A change takes effect from the review date only and does not apply retrospectively."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Cap applies","text":"If the index figure is higher than the limit in paragraph 2.1, the limit applies."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}],"48":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | Home-to-school transport: agreement | Page 48 of 70"},{"kind":"heading","num":"Schedule 6","text":"Performance and service credits"},{"kind":"clause","num":"1.1","title":"Performance standards","text":"The Supplier shall meet the Key Performance Indicators set out in Annex A to this Schedule."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Reporting","text":"The Supplier shall give the Council a performance report by the fifth (5th) Working Day of each month."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Audit","text":"The Council may audit the performance data on reasonable notice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.1","title":"Service Credits","text":"If the Supplier fails to meet a Key Performance Indicator in a month, the Council may deduct a Service Credit of 2% of the monthly Charges for each failure, up to a maximum of 10% of the monthly Charges.","clauseRef":"Schedule 6, paragraph 3.1","extractionIds":["X-C-012-serviceCredits"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.2","title":"Not a penalty","text":"Service Credits are a price adjustment that reflects the reduced value of the Services. They are not a penalty."},{"kind":"clause","num":"3.3","title":"Deduction","text":"Service Credits shall be deducted from the next invoice, or paid by the Supplier within thirty (30) days if no further invoice is due."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-012 | Tarnbrook Passenger Transport Ltd"}]}},"DOC-C-013":{"id":"DOC-C-013","contractId":"C-013","title":"School meals catering: agreement","pageCount":74,"isIllustrative":true,"pages":{"5":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | School meals catering: agreement | Page 5 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Contract Particulars"},{"kind":"item","num":"1","text":"Contracting Authority: Marchbank Borough Council."},{"kind":"item","num":"2","text":"Supplier: Dunmore Catering Services Ltd, company number 90011644."},{"kind":"item","num":"3","text":"Services: School meals catering."},{"kind":"item","num":"4","text":"Commencement Date: 1 September 2023.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 4","extractionIds":["X-C-013-startDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"5","text":"Expiry Date of the Initial Term: 31 August 2028.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 5","extractionIds":["X-C-013-endDate"]},{"kind":"item","num":"6","text":"Procurement route: Open procedure."},{"kind":"item","num":"7","text":"Governing law: the law of England and Wales."},{"kind":"item","num":"8","text":"Estimated annual value of the Services: £1,300,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 8","extractionIds":["X-C-013-estimatedAnnualValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"9","text":"Estimated total value over the Initial Term: £6,500,000 (excluding VAT).","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 9","extractionIds":["X-C-013-awardedTotalValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"10","text":"No maximum contract value is stated. The estimated total value above is the only value limit in the Agreement.","clauseRef":"Contract Particulars, item 10","extractionIds":["X-C-013-maximumValue"]},{"kind":"item","num":"11","text":"The estimated values in items 8 and 9 are provided for budgeting purposes only and do not oblige the Council to purchase any minimum volume of Services."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-013 | Dunmore Catering Services Ltd"}],"11":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | School meals catering: agreement | Page 11 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"2","text":"Term and extension"},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.1","title":"Term","text":"This Agreement starts on the Commencement Date and continues until the Expiry Date, unless it ends earlier under clause 30 or is extended under this clause 2."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.2","title":"Extension","text":"The Council may, by giving the Supplier written notice, extend the Term on 1 occasion by up to 12 months each time (each an Extension Period).","clauseRef":"Clause 2.2","extractionIds":["X-C-013-extensions"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.3","title":"Terms of an extension","text":"Each Extension Period is on the terms of this Agreement. The Charges for an Extension Period are reviewed only in accordance with Schedule 4."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.4","title":"Decision","text":"The decision to extend is the Council's alone. The Supplier may not refuse an extension that the Council has validly exercised."},{"kind":"clause","num":"2.5","title":"Longest possible Term","text":"The Term, including every Extension Period, cannot run beyond 31 August 2029."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-013 | Dunmore Catering Services Ltd"}],"18":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | School meals catering: agreement | Page 18 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"12","text":"Invoicing and payment"},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.1","title":"Invoices","text":"The Supplier shall invoice the Council monthly in arrears for Services properly performed."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.2","title":"Valid invoice","text":"A valid invoice shall quote the Council's purchase order number and the contract reference C-013, and shall be addressed to the Council's Accounts Payable team."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.3","title":"VAT","text":"The Charges are exclusive of VAT. The Council shall pay VAT at the rate in force on receipt of a valid VAT invoice."},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.4","title":"Payment","text":"The Council shall pay each undisputed invoice within 30 days of receipt.","clauseRef":"Clause 12.4","extractionIds":["X-C-013-paymentTerms"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"12.5","title":"Late payment","text":"Interest on late payment accrues under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-013 | Dunmore Catering Services Ltd"}],"29":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | School meals catering: agreement | Page 29 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"30","text":"Termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.1","title":"Termination for convenience","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time by giving the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice.","clauseRef":"Clause 30.1","extractionIds":["X-C-013-terminationForConvenience"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.2","title":"Termination for breach","text":"Either party may terminate this Agreement by written notice if the other commits a material breach that is not remedied within thirty (30) days of a notice requiring it to be remedied."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.3","title":"Insolvency","text":"The Council may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if the Supplier becomes insolvent or ceases to carry on business."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.4","title":"Required by law","text":"The Council may also terminate this Agreement by written notice if it is required to do so by law."},{"kind":"clause","num":"30.5","title":"Sums payable","text":"Where the Council terminates under clause 30.1, the only sums payable are those set out in clause 33.2."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-013 | Dunmore Catering Services Ltd"}],"30":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | School meals catering: agreement | Page 30 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"31","text":"Expiry, renewal and notice"},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.1","title":"Expiry and renewal","text":"The Council shall give the Supplier not less than three (3) months' written notice before the end of the Initial Term if it wishes to exercise an extension option or to let this Agreement expire.","clauseRef":"Clause 31.1","extractionIds":["X-C-013-noticePeriod","X-C-013-autoRenewal"]},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.2","title":"Serving notice","text":"Notice under clause 31.1 must be in writing and given in accordance with clause 45 (Notices)."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.3","title":"Expiry without notice","text":"If the Council gives no notice, this Agreement expires on the Expiry Date and the Supplier has no right to payment for Services after that date unless a Variation has been agreed under clause 41."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.4","title":"Last date for notice","text":"For the Initial Term, the last date on which the Council may give notice under clause 31.1 is 31 May 2028."},{"kind":"clause","num":"31.5","title":"Withdrawing a notice","text":"The Council may withdraw a notice to extend only with the Supplier's written agreement."},{"kind":"footer","text":"Execution version | Contract ref C-013 | Dunmore Catering Services Ltd"}],"31":[{"kind":"header","text":"Marchbank Borough Council | School meals catering: agreement | Page 31 of 74"},{"kind":"heading","num":"33","text":"Consequences of termination"},{"kind":"clause","num":"33.1","title":"Accrued rights","text":"Termination or expiry does not affect any right or liability that accrued before the d